# Tells vs Exitmania

When Dervis says **Tells**, he means **this repo** (`/Users/dervis/grid`, tells.team).
When he says **Exitmania**, he means `/Users/dervis/Developer/exitmania`.

Tells is **pre-launch** (password gate, no real customers). Engine identifiers migrate to `tells` now so the name does not calcify as GRID.

## Spoken / customer-facing

- Tells = org product (join, data, overwrites, later year-abo)
- Exitmania = public storefront + impulse commerce (this one **is** live)
- No third brand

New UI copy: **Tells**, not GRID.

## Code in this repo

- New and moved engine code lives under `lib/tells/`
- Do not add new `lib/tells/` files
- `GRID_*` env still works until Vercel aliases exist (`TELLS_*` may read the same value)
- Do not rename Tailwind `grid` layout classes
- Do not rename the git repo or `/e/` play URLs unless asked

## Code in Exitmania

Leave `grid_*` tables and routes (`grid_pilot_*`, `grid_checkout_*`, `GRID_PUBLIC_URL`). Exitmania has real bookings. That rename is a later, explicit job.

## Examples

- “Passwort-Gate auf Tells” → this repo, `/gate`
- “KIRA-Finale auf Exitmania” → Exitmania, `/m/kira/…`
